  <.collapse_information_component
    id="more-information-equalture"
    desc_paragraphs={[
      "After almost two years working with Go, I missed Elixir, especially the chance to try out new features like LiveView. That was one of my motivations for joining Equalture, along with the great experience I had with their game-based assessments during the hiring process.",
      "<strong>Equalture is a startup that provides a bias-free hiring platform</strong>. Based on game assessments, the platform analyzes teams and candidates, providing valuable insights into the best candidates for any team.",
      "As an Elixir developer, <strong>I developed new features on both the frontend and the backend of the product. While I mainly worked with Elixir and Phoenix LiveView, the project also involved other technologies like Kubernetes and Google Cloud.</strong>",
      "Some of my tasks included:",
      "<ul>",
      "<li>Developed a new API for external clients, proposing and maintaining its OpenAPI docs.</li>",
      "<li>Developed two-factor authentication (2FA) for the web app.</li>",
      "<li>Developed a real-time filter system for candidates, built on a multi-dimensional dynamic query.</li>",
      "<li>Led the DevOps area of the company, proposing and applying improvements to the Kubernetes cluster, such as using a default backend for maintenance pages and upgrading components like cert-manager and the NGINX ingress controller.</li>",
      "<li>Supported and mentored other team members, leading a team of three developers.</li>",
      "</ul>"
    ]}
